                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "272d9711-7b76-4d4c-86a9-846bd21dc6e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5631158-1dfa-34f9-8ee7-869566bd6e41",
                        "source_sense_id": "3c0ae386-3baa-3e77-b0e1-325d71c570da",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: nur im Meer vorkommendes, meist räuberisches Weichtier, dessen Mund mit Tentakeln umgeben ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "cephalopod",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cephalopod",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93c25a2a-6572-3b8c-8c0b-5ab0be638b81",
                                        "entry_id": "cd24256b-de81-3903-a1d1-4a45960099f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any mollusc of the class Cephalopoda, which includes squid, cuttlefish, octopus, nautiloids etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5115c794-2dfa-40f5-8ce4-0e87babcecf8",
                                                "sense_id": "93c25a2a-6572-3b8c-8c0b-5ab0be638b81",
                                                "text": "In terms of diversity, cephalopods include the egg case making argonauts, shelled nautiluses, venomous blue-ringed octopuses and enigmatic giants like the giant and colossal squid. […] Generally, cephalopod ink includes melanin, enzymes related to melanin production, catecholamines, peptidoglycans, free amino acids and metals (Derby 2014) ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c37d52a0-c196-471a-8f2a-5e7134e552a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5631158-1dfa-34f9-8ee7-869566bd6e41",
                        "source_sense_id": "3c0ae386-3baa-3e77-b0e1-325d71c570da",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: nur im Meer vorkommendes, meist räuberisches Weichtier, dessen Mund mit Tentakeln umgeben ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "céphalopode",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "céphalopode",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e10ee16-5ff1-32bc-b288-f9cf0887d343",
                                        "entry_id": "c01577c0-e9c5-387c-bc64-331b5c48f077",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mollusque marin dont la tête et la bouche sont garnies de tentacules."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3877cb33-8764-4f04-b087-aed966b2c70a",
                                                "sense_id": "5e10ee16-5ff1-32bc-b288-f9cf0887d343",
                                                "text": "Mis à part les nautiles, les céphalopodes actuels sont dépourvus de coquille externe. Les céphalopodes porteurs d'une coquille ont été autrefois beaucoup plus diversifiés, comme en témoignent les nombreux fossiles de céphalopodes comme les ammonites et le bélemnites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "céphalopode",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf36c40a-74fb-3fc7-9dcc-a21db1a1f4fb",
                                        "entry_id": "9bc8cc01-d19e-300c-9112-facc330fbd94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a le trait du céphalopode."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0402697c-12bb-4d2d-87a8-11514530cdbf",
                                                "sense_id": "bf36c40a-74fb-3fc7-9dcc-a21db1a1f4fb",
                                                "text": "La tête céphalopode penchait en avant, de telle façon que l’extrémité des tentacules faciaux couvrait l’arrière des gigantesques griffes avant et étreignait les genoux repliés du monstre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90884571-0525-4aa1-a2db-22ff6bcb42cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5631158-1dfa-34f9-8ee7-869566bd6e41",
